{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in one readable deterministic specification. The specification gives exactly one controllable action in each non-terminal decision state, is total on uncontrollables, forbids forward/random motion in obstacle-recovery states, uses short directed turns for ordinary recovery, and returns quickly to exploration when path_clear is observed. Action states self-loop on path_clear and only obstacle events preempt them, matching the stated runtime semantics.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion with simple universal plants.",
    "Use one deterministic policy specification with small helper commit states so each motion pulse is one-shot and obstacle recovery is conservative but coverage-oriented."
  ],
